[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3305787289","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110644#issuecomment-3305787289","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110644","id":3305787289,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FCk-Z","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-18T07:22:25Z","updated_at":"2025-09-18T07:22:25Z","body":"The `find_children()` method has an optional parameter `owned = true`, which prevents it from finding non-owned nodes by default. This helps avoid unexpected matches from other scenes instantiated in the current one (by default, it only searches within the current scene). Therefore, in the case of the root node, `find_children()` will not find any nodes unless you pass `owned = false` (the root node is not part of any scene file).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3305787289/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":1,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3305802115","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110644#issuecomment-3305802115","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110644","id":3305802115,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FComD","user":{"login":"lazzy-cipher","id":90345171,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwMzQ1MTcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90345171?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazzy-cipher","html_url":"https://github.com/lazzy-cipher","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazzy-cipher/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazzy-cipher/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazzy-cipher/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazzy-cipher/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazzy-cipher/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazzy-cipher/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazzy-cipher/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazzy-cipher/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazzy-cipher/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-18T07:25:21Z","updated_at":"2025-09-18T07:25:21Z","body":"> The `find_children()` method has an optional parameter `owned = true`, which prevents it from finding non-owned nodes by default. This helps avoid unexpected matches from other scenes instantiated in the current one (by default, it only searches within the current scene). Therefore, in the case of the root node, `find_children()` will not find any nodes unless you pass `owned = false` (the root node is not part of any scene file).\n\nThat was it! Seems like a documentation issue, I'll make a PR.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.